.\" Manpage for fix-touch.sh
.TH FIX-TOUCH.SH 1 "August 2024" "1.0" "Bash Scripts"
.SH NAME
fix-touch.sh \- Adjust touchscreen settings and rotate display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./fix-touch.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfix-touch.sh\fR script is used to adjust touchscreen calibration and rotate the display on a Linux system. 
It rotates the primary display to the right and applies a coordinate transformation matrix to the touchscreen.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
This script requires:
.TP
.B xrandr
.TP
.B xinput

.SH USAGE
Run the script without arguments:
.PP
.B ./fix-touch.sh
.PP
This command will:
.TP
1. Rotate the primary display to the right.
.TP
2. Apply a coordinate transformation matrix to the touchscreen.

.SH AUTHOR
Written by AnAnnoyinGoose.

